From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:14:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 128/130] Status bar: recount after a typing pause, cache
 selection counts

Typing no longer recounts the whole text on every key: the bar keeps the
last counts and counts again 300 ms after the last edit. Open and reload
still count at once. The selection size is cached per tab by text
generation and selection ends, and above 2 MB selected it shows the line
count only.

The edit fingerprint now runs only in the focused text box and skips
modifier and navigation keys; over a huge range it compares the line
count and cursor line instead of treating every key as an edit. Tab in a
Markdown table or list reports an edit, as it can reformat other rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

